3}(9)+(0) & =3 \\\\ 3+0 & =3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓ \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}(0)+(3) & =3 \\\\ 0+3 & =3 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,$\\frac{1}{3}y+x=3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=-3x+9.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,9)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9) & =-3(0)+9 \\\\ 9 & =9\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =-3(3)+9 \\\\ 0 & =-9+9 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3x+9$ is  an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nAll the given equations represented the line in the graph. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\"" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501330 1080 "II and III only" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501330 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501330 1083 #uuid "bae18ee6-b3b9-5327-ad96-6d55d7e27bdc" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501331 1080 "II only" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501331 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501331 1083 #uuid "cf447eac-1836-54a3-8082-5758760bcbed" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501316 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501319 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501320 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501325 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501330 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1077 "selection" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1078 #edb/ref 17592186501316 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501332 1079 #uuid "e1108d84-a4e2-5397-a2f7-9adbc9f6a9b9" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501333 1080 "I, II and III" 13194139535373 17592186045443 true] [17592186501333 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 131